range 8346877c..2cd02823 (U4-late1; engine branch-scoped)
The review of `2026-09-26-init-commits-the-lock` against `develop` found 10 issues. The scope was 18 commits plus uncommitted plan-log changes, with the generated uv sidecar lock and the run logs skimmed only. The most serious is the second Python pin. It can make the committed lock drop a Python project's own Python version, and CI then fails at install.

Findings 2, 3, 5, 6 and 7 overlap gaps the plan's own round-2 review already logged in `index.md` (G1–G5 plus the R2 docs note). The site-doc half of finding 7 is also assigned to the still-pending docs unit U5. They are kept here because they are still open in this diff.

